<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Inflation in the UK has risen, putting hou=
seholds under renewed financial pressure.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The consumer prices index, which measures =
the cost of goods and services across the economy, has risen to 3.1% in the=
 year to August, up from 2.9% in July.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">On a monthly basis, CPI rose by 0.5% in Au=
gust, driven by =E2=80=9Ctransport, particularly motor fuels=E2=80=9D, the =
Office for National Statistics (ONS) said.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Motor fuel prices across the UK soared by =
23% in the 12 months to August, today=E2=80=99s inflation report shows.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">That is up from 15.5% in the year to July,=
 with petrol prices hitting their highest level since November 2022.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The ONS reports that the average price of =
petrol rose by 9.1p a litre between July and August, to an average price of=
 161.3p a litre.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Diesel prices rose by 14.2p a litre in Aug=
ust, to an average of 181.8p a litre.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Air fares rose by 6.2% between July and Au=
gust 2026, the inflation report shows.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">This was mainly down to long-haul routes, =
where fares rose in August 2026 compared with a fall a year ago.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Worryingly, the cost of goods produced by =
UK factories rose at a faster rate in August, too.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Producer output prices =E2=80=93 or the co=
st of goods at the =E2=80=9Cfactory gate=E2=80=9D =E2=80=93 rose by 3.7% in=
 the year to August, up from 3.3% in July.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The ONS reports that the 12-month inflatio=
n rate for food and non-alcoholic beverages was 1.3% in August 2026, unchan=
ged from July. It was last lower than this in September 2021.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Prices of chocolate confectionery rose by =
less than a year ago, while meat prices fell slightly in August.</p>
